# C11 event-source inject — DO NOT APPLY

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Base: origin/cursor/c11-profile-orders-lookup-e504 6272cd2d16957959397ebf68b94a8e1447bdf6c0
Branch: cursor/c11-event-source-inject-e504

DO NOT APPLY this hunk. Do not edit App/AppSession.swift, App/AppCompositionRoot.swift, or Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj from this branch.

## Where the rows are

No original-event read on this branch returns already loaded `[OriginalAuditEvent]` rows.
`SupportEventLocator` only reads an `OriginalEventSource` the caller passes in.
`InMemoryOriginalEventSource` exists only in tests.

The signed-in order reads are only on AppSession:

- `ownedOrderReader` / `currentOwnedOrderSession` / `ownedOrderSignedInIdentity` (around line 3096)
- `profileReader` (around line 3113)
- `orderLifecycleReader` / `orderLifecycleJournal` (`orders-v1.json` reservations, not original audit rows)

Those readers return `ProfileOrder` or `OrderLifecycleDetail` on demand. They do not store original audit rows. Do not synthesize `OriginalAuditEvent` from `ProfileOrder`. Do not call an admin audit-log API.

## What the page can call

`Core/ProfileOrderEventSourceInjection.swift` accepts an explicit source.

- Rows present: pass them into the existing `SupportLookupEntry.lookupByOrderId`. The request's first ORDER id must equal the opened order. A different id is `originalMissing`.
- Source absent (`nil`): `entry()` and `lookupOpenedOrder` return nil, `lookups` stays 0, and nothing is sent.

```swift
var injection = ProfileOrderEventSourceInjection(events: loadedOriginalOrderEvents)
if let entry = injection.entry() {
    orderSupport = ProfileOrderSupportLookup(entry: entry, currentProjection: nil)
}
let opened = try injection.lookupOpenedOrder(openedOrderID)
```

`loadedOriginalOrderEvents` is not a member of AppSession. Until a real array is passed, the orders page keeps `orderSupport == nil` and stays quiet.

## Withheld call site (signed-in orders host)

File: `App/OwnedOrderComposition.swift` `SessionOwnedOrdersView`
Do not apply. AppSession has no original-event array to pass.

```
         ProfileOrdersView(reader: session.ownedOrderReader, ticketReader: session.ticketWalletReader)
+            orderSupport stays nil while loadedOriginalOrderEvents is absent
```

